  "question": {
    "text": "The IUPAC name of the following molecule is\r\n<img src=\"assets\\qt0039_8d3d4f6233bf.png\">"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "5,6 -dimethyihept-2-ene",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "2,3 -dimethyhept-5-ene",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "5,6 -dimethyhept-3-ene",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$5-$ iso-propylhex-2-ene",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0039_54d114d1a205.png\">\r\n\r\nThe longest chain contains 7 C-atom, so the root word is hept and suffix -ene is added for double bond along with its position. Since, two methyl goups are also present at 5 and 6 positions, so the correct IUPAC name of the compound is 5.6 -dimethylhept-2-ene."
  }
